    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "53 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-53"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.24",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under section 34AB of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 continues in force, after that commencement, as:\n\n(a) an appointment under section 34AB of that Act (as amended\nby this Act); and\n\n(b) if the appointment is in respect of a Federal Magistrate—an\nappointment in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 34AB(2) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under Division 3 of Part III of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979 before the commencement of this\nitem has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or\nin relation to, a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an\nissuing authority, under that Division.\nBankruptcy Act 1966",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under section 34AB of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 continues in force, after that commencement, as:\n\n(a) an appointment under section 34AB of that Act (as amended\nby this Act); and\n\n(b) if the appointment is in respect of a Federal Magistrate—an\nappointment in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 34AB(2) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under Division 3 of Part III of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979 before the commencement of this\nitem has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or\nin relation to, a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an\nissuing authority, under that Division.\nBankruptcy Act 1966",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-53-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-53-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "275b59c18833b5d61ae2212131914cc3a8519d82a460db174e51fe28e71c2082",
      "skos:note": "Appointment and consent continuity after commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-53",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "53 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 24,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under section 34AB of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 continues in force, after that commencement, as:\n\n(a) an appointment under section 34AB of that Act (as amended\nby this Act); and\n\n(b) if the appointment is in respect of a Federal Magistrate—an\nappointment in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 34AB(2) of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under Division 3 of Part III of the Australian Security\nIntelligence Organisation Act 1979 before the commencement of this\nitem has effect, after that commencement, as if it had been done by, or\nin relation to, a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an\nissuing authority, under that Division.\nBankruptcy Act 1966"
    },
    {
