    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-106-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "106 4  Saving—Federal Magistrates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-106-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.33",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An appointment that is in force immediately before the\ncommencement of this section under subsection 105.2(1) in respect\nof a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as an appointment in respect of a Judge of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia under that subsection.\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\n(2) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this section under subsection 105.2(2) in respect of a Federal\nMagistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a\nconsent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n\n(3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an\nissuing authority for continued preventative detention orders, under\nDivision 105 before the commencement of this section has effect,\nafter that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation\nto, a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing\nauthority for continued preventative detention orders, under that\nDivision.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An appointment that is in force immediately before the\ncommencement of this section under subsection 105.2(1) in respect\nof a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as an appointment in respect of a Judge of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia under that subsection.\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\n(2) A consent that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this section under subsection 105.2(2) in respect of a Federal\nMagistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a\nconsent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n\n(3) A thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an\nissuing authority for continued preventative detention orders, under\nDivision 105 before the commencement of this section has effect,\nafter that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation\nto, a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing\nauthority for continued preventative detention orders, under that\nDivision.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-106-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-106-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-106-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "73ed31f1bcbf1b8c3bbc6ad3b60a5cdf1f7cf5a31491464b3ddf30473598720c"
