    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-233",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "233 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-233"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 45A(1) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect of a\nFederal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a\nconsent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 45A(2) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect\nof a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as\na nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nExtradition Act 1988 before the commencement of this item has effect,\nafter that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an\neligible Federal Circuit Court Judge under that Act.\nFair Work Act 2009",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 45A(1) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect of a\nFederal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a\nconsent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 45A(2) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect\nof a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as\na nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nExtradition Act 1988 before the commencement of this item has effect,\nafter that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an\neligible Federal Circuit Court Judge under that Act.\nFair Work Act 2009",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-233-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-233-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e713840515c61b61caea37c9f81eb8a2566f9967e67330028f9e0da144b7041d",
      "skos:note": "Consent and nomination continuity after commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-233",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "233 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 45A(1) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect of a\nFederal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as a\nconsent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 45A(2) of the Extradition Act 1988 in respect\nof a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that commencement, as\na nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of\nAustralia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nExtradition Act 1988 before the commencement of this item has effect,\nafter that commencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an\neligible Federal Circuit Court Judge under that Act.\nFair Work Act 2009"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-233-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
