    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "417 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-417"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.67",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 38ZC(1) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nMatters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force,\nafter that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 38ZC(2) of the Mutual Assistance in\nCriminal Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nMutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an eligible Federal Circuit Court\nJudge under that Act.\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 38ZC(1) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nMatters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force,\nafter that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 38ZC(2) of the Mutual Assistance in\nCriminal Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nMutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an eligible Federal Circuit Court\nJudge under that Act.\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b27639998960a05b574300f53000685fe42ca6e890e821ac81881b9c819623ca",
      "skos:note": "Consent and nomination continue in force after commencement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-417",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "417 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 67,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 38ZC(1) of the Mutual Assistance in Criminal\n\nSchedule 1  Main amendments\n\nMatters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force,\nafter that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the\nFederal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 38ZC(2) of the Mutual Assistance in\nCriminal Matters Act 1987 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate under the\nMutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act 1987 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an eligible Federal Circuit Court\nJudge under that Act.\nNational Consumer Credit Protection Act 2009"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-417"
