    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-459",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "459 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-459"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.72",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 91(1) of the National Vocational Education and\nTraining Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of\na Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 91(2) of the National Vocational Education\nand Training Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect\nof a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Division 2 of\nPart 5 of the National Vocational Education and Training Regulator Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an issuing\nofficer under that Division.\nOmbudsman Act 1976",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 91(1) of the National Vocational Education and\nTraining Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of\na Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 91(2) of the National Vocational Education\nand Training Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect\nof a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Division 2 of\nPart 5 of the National Vocational Education and Training Regulator Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an issuing\nofficer under that Division.\nOmbudsman Act 1976",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-459-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-459-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "5dcc2c1c2e28eead5c12d4251ebfb60a59f5c7f3a62411b5a994fcde05a955a5",
      "skos:note": "Consent and nomination continue in force after commencement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-459",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "459 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 72,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 91(1) of the National Vocational Education and\nTraining Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of\na Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 91(2) of the National Vocational Education\nand Training Regulator Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect\nof a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Division 2 of\nPart 5 of the National Vocational Education and Training Regulator Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, an issuing\nofficer under that Division.\nOmbudsman Act 1976"
    },
    {
