    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "514 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-514"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.80",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under subsection 6DB(1) of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as an appointment in\nrespect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under that\nsubsection.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 6DB(2) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing authority, under\nthat Act.\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under subsection 6DB(1) of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as an appointment in\nrespect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under that\nsubsection.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 6DB(2) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing authority, under\nthat Act.\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "b1b46738cf140951882d3efbcaee894b19c46b3e9c13cba0c43cf30bdb354aaa",
      "skos:note": "Continuation of appointments and consents"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-514",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "514 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 80,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nAn appointment that is in force immediately before the commencement\nof this item under subsection 6DB(1) of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate\ncontinues in force, after that commencement, as an appointment in\nrespect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia under that\nsubsection.\n(2)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 6DB(2) of the Telecommunications (Interception\nand Access) Act 1979 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in\nforce, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nauthority, under the Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act\n1979 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing authority, under\nthat Act.\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-514-norm",
      "@type": "values:Undertaking",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
