    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-550",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "550 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-550"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.84",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 96(1) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 96(2) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Part 6 of the\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an issuing officer under that Part.\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nTobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 96(1) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 96(2) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Part 6 of the\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an issuing officer under that Part.\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nTobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-550-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-550-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9cbe26bcd5540674b73e9ea2668b7c6d14810a72c2e9d1a56241b84407153d44",
      "skos:note": "Consent and nomination continuity after commencement"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-550",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "550 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 84,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 96(1) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 96(2) of the Tertiary Education Quality and\nStandards Agency Act 2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues\nin force, after that commencement, as a nomination in respect of a\nJudge of the Federal Circuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a magistrate under Part 6 of the\nTertiary Education Quality and Standards Agency Act 2011 before the\ncommencement of this item has effect, after that commencement, as if it\nhad been done by, or in relation to, an issuing officer under that Part.\n\nMain amendments  Schedule 1\n\nTobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011"
    },
    {
