    {
      "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-555",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "555 Saving provisions",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-555"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013.pdf, p.85",
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 79(1) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011\nin respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 79(2) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nofficer, under Part 2 of Chapter 4 of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing officer, under that\nPart.\nTrans-Tasman Proceedings Act 2010",
      "skos:definition": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 79(1) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011\nin respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 79(2) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nofficer, under Part 2 of Chapter 4 of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing officer, under that\nPart.\nTrans-Tasman Proceedings Act 2010",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-555-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013-sch-1-sec-555-logic-alleninterval-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c2d847d4779af8df54bcd382c09fd4f75928daed79ba9594ef1f039f5c09138d",
      "skos:note": "Consent and nomination continuity"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/federal-circuit-court-of-australia-consequential-amendments-act-2013#sch-1-sec-555",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "555 Saving provisions",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 85,
      "values:originalText": "(1)\nA consent that is in force immediately before the commencement of this\nitem under subsection 79(1) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act 2011\nin respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a consent in respect of a Judge of the Federal Circuit\nCourt of Australia.\n(2)\nA nomination that is in force immediately before the commencement of\nthis item under subsection 79(2) of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 in respect of a Federal Magistrate continues in force, after that\ncommencement, as a nomination in respect of a Judge of the Federal\nCircuit Court of Australia.\n(3)\nA thing done by, or in relation to, a Federal Magistrate, as an issuing\nofficer, under Part 2 of Chapter 4 of the Tobacco Plain Packaging Act\n2011 before the commencement of this item has effect, after that\ncommencement, as if it had been done by, or in relation to, a Judge of\nthe Federal Circuit Court of Australia, as an issuing officer, under that\nPart.\nTrans-Tasman Proceedings Act 2010"
    },
